    <footnotes>
        <footnote id="F1">Reflects the 5,098 Class A ordinary shares of the registrant that are included in the 5,098 private placement units of the registrant purchased by BHAV Partners II LLC (the &quot;Sponsor&quot;) on November 12, 2026 in connection with the underwriters' partial exercise of their over-allotment option. Each private placement unit was purchased for $10.00 per unit and consists of one Class A ordinary share and one right to receive one-fourth (1/4) of one Class A ordinary share upon consummation of the registrant's initial business combination.</footnote>
        <footnote id="F2">The reporting owner, the Sponsor, in whose name the securities reported herein are held, is managed by its managing member, Giri Devanur. Mr. Devanur is also the Chief Executive Officer and director of the registrant. Mr. Devanur holds voting and investment discretion with respect to the securities held of record by the Sponsor. Mr. Devanur may be deemed a beneficial owner of securities held by the Sponsor but he disclaims beneficial ownership of any such securities except to the extent of his pecuniary interest therein.</footnote>
        <footnote id="F3">Each right converts automatically into one-fourth (1/4) of one Class A ordinary share upon consummation of the registrant's initial business combination, subject to certain adjustments described in the rights agreement governing the rights. No fractional Class A ordinary shares will be issued upon conversion of such rights. If the initial business combination is not consummated within the applicable time period specified in the registrant's amended and restated memorandum and articles of association, as currently in effect, the rights shall expire and shall be worthless.</footnote>
        <footnote id="F4">Represents the 1,274 Class A ordinary shares (reflecting the rounding down of 1,274.5 shares) issuable upon conversion of the 5,098 rights included in the private placement units purchased by the Sponsor on November 12, 2026, upon consummation of the registrant's initial business combination. Following the reported transaction, the Sponsor holds 230,098 rights, which will convert into an aggregate of 57,524 Class A ordinary shares (reflecting the rounding down of 57,524.50 shares to the nearest whole share, as no fractional Class A ordinary shares will be issued upon conversion of the rights).</footnote>
    </footnotes>

